WHAT IT DOES. forced_v3_verdict adds a knife-edge row's two columns, in parentheses and '; '-joined, to the burst test's part of
the reason, in all three forms of it: after the evidence and the centroid for BACKGROUND SOURCE; after "no cataloged source is
identified as their emitter" for NOT CENTERED ON THE TARGET (source not identified); after the lower-cased verdict for every
other result. The columns:
  mc_draws    the published verdict as the most frequent outcome of the 20 draws, its named sources and its fraction, e.g.
              "CONSISTENT WITH A BACKGROUND SOURCE (VLSSr J105425.8+715204, VLSSr J105246.5+715924) in 14 of 20 Monte Carlo
              draws"; a tie (published UNDECIDED): "a tie of 20 Monte Carlo draws, 10 each: <outcome>; <outcome>"
  knife_edge  the statistic that put the row on its threshold (the default draw's), e.g. "knife-edge: centroid z 3.02 vs 3,
              Monte Carlo error 0.017"
The verdicts and their mapping (V3_MAP) are unchanged. A row without the columns, or with them empty (every unflagged row),
gives exactly today's (verdict, reason). The figures of a run show the text once they are redrawn after the republish (the
figure step reads the run's file when it draws).
